<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Evaluate</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>evaluate &lt;item&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>evaluate helmet
</pre>
<p>Have a close look at something you can wear or wield. You are told:
</p>
<ul><li>how much it weighs;</li>
<li>what size of person it was made to fit, so you know before you try it on</li></ul>
<pre> whether it will be too big or too small;
</pre>
<ul><li>what condition it is in, from like new to badly worn;</li>
<li>what it would take to refit it to your size: tailoring for clothes, leather</li></ul>
<pre> work for leather, metal work for metal armour, shields and weapons 
 (see <a cmd='#'>Help Resize</a>).
</pre>
<p>Anyone can evaluate; you don't need to practice it. Some blacksmiths will also evaluate the quality of weapons, armour and shields for you: see the sign at the smithy.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Resize</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wear</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Appraisal</a>
</pre>




</div>